The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/equipment-hvac/equip-hvac-11-speed-control-modes-completeness.md`.

Summary of findings:

- **7 total findings**: 1 high, 3 medium, 3 low
- **High**: `TwoSpeedAlternating` lacks the minimum-time-per-speed guard that the other two 2-speed modes have, risking speed oscillation when speeds are dynamically disabled
- **Medium**: `VariableSpeedIdeal` and `MultiSpeedInterpolated` use identical interpolation (differ only in side effects); 3-speed equipment falls to SingleSpeed in `cooling_speed_control_mode()`; `HeatPumpHeaterConfig` missing symmetric `heating_speed_control_mode()`
- **Low**: `er_stages` config has no staged-backup runtime logic (same as OCHRE), fragile fresh-cycle reset in `TwoSpeedTime`, silent zero-capacity edge case in `capacity_fractions_for`

On the two specific questions asked: (1) backup heat staging is handled at the control layer, not in these speed-control files — no staging hierarchy conflict found here; (2) variable-speed mode **does** interpolate between stages (not snap to discrete speeds), but the name `VariableSpeedIdeal` is misleading since it uses the same discrete-stage interpolation as `MultiSpeedInterpolated` rather than a true ideal-capacity algorithm.
